journal">Assmann SF, Pocock SJ, Enos LE, Kasten LE. Subgroup analysis and other (mis)uses of baseline data in clinical trials. <source>Lancet</source><year>2000</year>;<volume>355</volume>:<fpage>1064</fpage>-9.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10744093</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref46"><label>46</label><citation citation-type="journal">Chan AW, Tetzlaff J, Altman DG, G&#x000f8;tzsche PC, Hr&#x000f3;bjartsson A, Krle&#x0017e;a-Jeric K, et al. The SPIRIT initiative: defining standard protocol items for randomised trials. <source>German J Evid Quality Health Care (suppl)</source><year>2008</year>;<volume>102</volume>:<fpage>S27</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="ref47"><label>47</label><citation citation-type="journal">MacLean CH, Morton SC, Ofman JJ, Roth EA, Shekelle PG. How useful are unpublished data from the Food and Drug Administration in meta-analysis? <source>J Clin Epidemiol</source><year>2003</year>;<volume>56</volume>:<fpage>44</fpage>-51.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12589869</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref48"><label>48</label><citation citation-type="journal">Turner EH. A taxpayer-funded clinical trials registry and results database. <source>PLoS Med</source><year>2004</year>;<volume>1</volume>:<fpage>e60</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15562322</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref49"><label>49</label><citation citation-type="journal">Laine C, Horton R, DeAngelis CD, Drazen JM, Frizelle FA, Godlee F, et al. Clinical trial registration&#x02014;looking back and moving ahead. <source>N Engl J Med</source><year>2007</year>;<volume>356</volume>:<fpage>2734</fpage>-6.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17548427</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref50"><label>50</label><citation citation-type="journal">Sim I, Chan AW, Gulmezoglu AM, Evans T, Pang T. Clinical trial registration: transparency is the watchword. <source>Lancet</source><year>2006</year>;<volume>367</volume>:<fpage>1631</fpage>-3.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16714166</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref51"><label>51</label><citation citation-type="journal">Krle&#x0017e;a-Jeric K, Chan AW, Dickersin K, Sim I, Grimshaw J, Gluud C. Principles for international registration of protocol information and results from human trials of health related interventions: Ottawa statement (part 1). <source>BMJ</source><year>2005</year>;<volume>330</volume>:<fpage>956</fpage>-8.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15845980</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list><notes notes-type="citation-text"><p><bold>Cite this as: </bold> <italic>BMJ</italic> 2008;337:a2299</p></notes></back></article>